            <ArticleTitle>Dismiss Systematic Transrectal Ultrasound-guided and Embrace Targeted Magnetic Resonance Imaging-informed Prostate Biopsy: Is the Paradigm Ready to Shift?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.eururo.2015.05.049</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0302-2838(15)00455-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Multiparametric magnetic resonance imaging-informed prostate biopsy is attracting increasing interest among practicing urologists. Whether this will become the new gold standard in prostate cancer diagnosis and supplant systematic transrectal ultrasound-guided sampling remains to be determined. Here we present the main open questions and current concerns regarding this new approach.</AbstractText>
